# `./run-demo test --mutants` is the command that promise names. IT HAS
# NEVER RUN. It is not implemented here and nothing under demo/ implements
# it either. The build handed over anyway, and no evidence surface recorded
# the gap — which is the actual defect. A refusal that only this file can
# see is a gap disclosed to nobody.
#
# WHAT WAS DONE INSTEAD, AND WHY. Implementing the pass honestly means
# sixteen anchored source edits across roughly ten files this launcher does
# not own, each with a mapping from a plan criterion to a test node id, and
# a mutant that cannot be anchored has to fail the run rather than be
# skipped — otherwise the mutation pass becomes the very thing §8.2 was
# written against. That is a work item, not a launcher fix. So the gap is
# made LOUD instead, in the two places a reader actually looks:
#
#   1. the flag itself says plainly that it is not implemented, names what
#      IS known about each mutant, and still refuses (exit 2) so it can
#      never pass vacuously; and
#   2. EVERY `./run-demo test` prints the same disclosure immediately
#      above its summary line — so the run that produces "N passed" is the
